00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:27.270
Nicholas wrote in about the RNC withdrawing
from the Commission on Presidential Debates,

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:31.430
something we talked about previously, as well
as earlier this week.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:35.289
Nicola said Hear me out, have a debate.

00:05:35.289 --> 00:05:38.699
That's just a Democrat and a third party.

00:05:38.699 --> 00:05:45.479
Imagine if you had Biden or some Democrat
and Justin Amash debating and just left Republicans

00:05:45.479 --> 00:05:46.479
out of it.

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:50.020
The RNC would be like, No, you weren't supposed
to do that, and it would be amazing.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:54.229
Yeah, I've been thinking about this a lot,
and this even came up on our bonus show discussion

00:05:54.229 --> 00:06:00.580
earlier this week about Republicans seemingly
bailing on presidential debates.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:06.830
The idea of Republicans is to delegitimize
or delegate a mate.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:07.830
Whoa.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:13.689
The presidential debates by saying they are
biased and the Commission on Presidential

00:06:13.689 --> 00:06:15.660
Debates is Partizan.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.240
And we're just getting out.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:22.529
And they're imagining, of course, that that
would leave only the Democratic nominee and

00:06:22.529 --> 00:06:24.750
that there would just be no debates whatsoever.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:30.969
It is true that if you had, you know, I've
always said, I want third parties to have

00:06:30.969 --> 00:06:32.899
more of a presence in American politics.

00:06:32.899 --> 00:06:41.059
If you had a stronger third party candidate
or multiple candidates and the commission

00:06:41.059 --> 00:06:47.219
organized legitimate debates where you had
the Democratic nominee, as well as those third

00:06:47.219 --> 00:06:48.610
party candidates.

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:51.270
It might make the RNC lose their mind.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.699
That's absolutely true.

00:06:52.699 --> 00:07:00.240
The risk, of course, is that because there's
no Republican in the presidential debates,

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.909
very few Republicans even watch it.

00:07:02.909 --> 00:07:07.919
You have a Democrat with a couple of third
party candidates, and all it serves to do

00:07:07.919 --> 00:07:13.279
is to siphon off some voters from the Democratic
candidate to those third party candidates.

00:07:13.279 --> 00:07:15.580
So I think it is not a strategy without risk.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:20.590
It would absolutely trigger Republicans to
be left out, for sure.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.279
It might be to their benefit.

00:07:22.279 --> 00:07:26.599
And so I think it has to be thought through
very carefully.

00:07:26.599 --> 00:07:31.539
Harb wrote in with an idea for a different
five day workweek.

00:07:31.539 --> 00:07:34.900
Now we've been talking a lot about the four
day workweek, the four day workweek.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:38.999
The idea is you have a four day workweek and
a three day weekend.

00:07:38.999 --> 00:07:42.899
Every week you do a little bit of adjustment
of hours, you do a little bit of adjustment

00:07:42.899 --> 00:07:47.969
of expectations and you sort of like more
or less get the same amount of work done in

00:07:47.969 --> 00:07:50.720
information type, jobs, knowledge, jobs.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:55.319
This doesn't work when it's about a retail
store being open, as you would in a five day

00:07:55.319 --> 00:07:56.319
workweek.

00:07:56.319 --> 00:08:02.491
Harb has a different idea, which is a five
day workweek, which is three days on, two

00:08:02.491 --> 00:08:05.879
days off, so the weekends move.

00:08:05.879 --> 00:08:11.520
And the idea would be you do three 10 hour
days and then you get two days off.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:16.169
And then you get another three 10 hour days
and then you get two days off, so the two

00:08:16.169 --> 00:08:22.159
days off shift throughout the week, it's a
little complicated, but the idea is that you

00:08:22.159 --> 00:08:28.860
end up working a little more each year, but
you also have more days off each year, and

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:33.650
this will allow people to have both weekdays
off and weekends off.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:39.150
I think it's really interesting and there's
a lot of sense in it, and I've heard proposals

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.830
like this before.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:46.330
The difficulty is it does become a nightmare
for child care.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:50.580
It becomes a nightmare for a lot of different
things where you have to know, OK, if I'm

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:54.500
making a doctor's appointment for six months
in advance, is this the week where I have

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.320
Wednesday and Thursday off?

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.730
Or is this the week where I have Saturday
and Sunday off?

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:00.940
So there's a lot of complexities to it.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.020
That's not a reason not to do it.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:07.600
But it seems very difficult to imagine that
the working world at large is going to be

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.100
interested in such a proposal.

